# CODEOWNERS for rore/agent-workflow
#
# Default owner: @rore. Any file in the repo that doesn't have a
# more-specific rule below gets routed to the maintainer for review.
#
# Self-protecting paths are listed explicitly so an agent can't drop
# the default rule and silently slip a governance-config change past
# review:
#   - agent-redline-policy.yaml      (the redline policy itself)
#   - agent-workflow.yaml            (per-repo workflow config)
#   - .github/workflows/             (the CI gates)
#   - core/schema/                   (cross-install JSON contracts)
#   - core/agent-redline/core/schema/
#   - docs/SPEC.md                   (normative spec)
#   - .agent-redline/suppressions.yaml
#
# When the redline reporter's `review.checkpoints_satisfied` predicate
# evaluates `codeownerApproval` it consumes the intersection of:
#   (a) approvals on the PR (state = APPROVED), and
#   (b) the codeowner set GitHub computes from this file.
# Branch protection's "Require Code Owner review" rule, when on, also
# enforces this intersection.

* @rore

# Self-protecting paths — explicit override to make the review intent
# visible even when scanning the file.
agent-redline-policy.yaml              @rore
agent-workflow.yaml                    @rore
.github/workflows/                     @rore
.github/CODEOWNERS                     @rore
core/schema/                           @rore
core/agent-redline/core/schema/        @rore
docs/SPEC.md                           @rore
.agent-redline/suppressions.yaml       @rore
